 "notes": "A3 force-window task assets -> <p2p_root>/assets/urdf/force_window/{objects,fixtures}/ + meta.json (own meta, not\nContactBench's). Run with any python that has numpy + trimesh:  python make_fw_assets.py <p2p_root>\n\nFragile grasp (\"fw_fragile_m<g>\"): a 66 mm x 100 mm cylinder (\"thin-walled can\"; one convex collision mesh) standing on\na 150 x 150 x 4 mm coaster fixture. Mass variants (hidden per env via precise_assembly.multi_problems): 80 / 110 / 150 /\n200 g, same shape, so the slip force (minimum grip) differs per env and can't be seen. Goal: lift 10 cm.\n\nPress to force (\"fw_press_k<k>\"): a rocker key. Fixture = base block 60 x 40 x 30 mm. Object = lever 80 x 20 x 6 mm,\npivot (revolute JointSpec, axis +y) at its back end, a 12 mm dome pad on top at r = 64 mm from the pivot. Return spring\nk (N m / rad) differs per variant (hidden per env); the target force F* = 4 N then sits at angle F* r / k.\nLower stop 0 deg (rest), upper stop 20 deg (past the widest break angle).\n"
